# The answer lane: a calendar whose policy says "stack" for a verb asks
# this stack BEFORE committing, with @calendar.phase == "answer". Absent
# or false @calendar.res.ok is a 403 to the client; `code` maps to an HTTP
# status (cannot 403 | limit 507 | unavailable 503) and `msg` is what the
# client shows. Here: an event put into the demo calendar must recur
# daily — the shape this stack knows how to run.
WHEN @calendar.phase == "answer" && @calendar.op == "put" && @calendar.event.recur.freq != "DAILY"
  EMIT @calendar.res.ok = false,
       @calendar.res.code = "cannot",
       @calendar.res.msg = "this calendar holds daily schedules; give the event a daily repeat"
